Analysis
The story is told from the third person point of view, and is mostly made up of declarative sentences. The sentences are also mostly simple, which makes the story easy to follow, despite the seemingly random order of events. The story uses many repetitions, both in words and sentences, which add to the feeling of the unrestrained and primitive life of the people living in the woods. The use of the present tense brings the story to the present, making the events feel immediate and giving the story a timeless quality.

